#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run one agy (or OpenCode) task headlessly in an isolated git worktree and report honestly.

  agy-task start  SLUG [--model M] [--effort E] [--agent NAME] [--max-denied 10] [--max-tool-errors 20] [--timeout 20m] [--base REF] [--setup CMD] [--review] [--yolo] [--wait] PROMPT|-
  agy-task resume SLUG [--timeout 20m] [--review] [--yolo] PROMPT|-
  agy-task list
  agy-task clean  SLUG [--force]

start and resume run only under Claude Code (CLAUDECODE=1) or with SWARMKIT_ALLOW_WORKERS=1; list and clean run anywhere.

--review is for tasks that answer in text: ok then means "no tool denied and a non-empty
response", not "files changed". --setup CMD runs in the worktree before agy (e.g. installing
or linking dependencies; a fresh worktree has tracked files only). At most $AGY_TASK_MAX
(default 3) tasks run at once; --wait queues for a free slot instead of refusing.
Gated by default (see "agy gate" below): agy reads and edits worktree files only, and its shell is
limited to read-only commands (none under --agent), so run tests and builds yourself on the branch.
--yolo auto-approves every tool and is NOT sandboxed (agy can then write outside the worktree and
reach the network); use it only for trusted work.
Everything lands under $AGY_TASK_DIR (default ~/.agy-tasks/<repo>/<slug>): the worktree,
result.json and agy.log. agy's own "status" is SUCCESS even when tools were denied, so
result.json carries a recomputed "ok".
Git isolation: a worktree's .git is a file the worker can rewrite. The gitdir is recorded at creation and
every later git call in the worktree is pinned to it, after checking it against the main repo's own record
(no fsmonitor, hooks, ext-diff, textconv or system config; attributes from the base commit). A run that
changed .git (restored), created a nested .git or .gitmodules, or changed the main repo's git config, hooks,
info/ or worktree record is NOT ok and not auto-committed. Run agy-task from the main checkout, never
from inside a task dir. Scope: this keeps the wrapper's own git calls from running what a worker planted
through file edits. It is not a sandbox: the runner allowlist (npm test etc.) runs worker-written code on
the host. An OS-level sandbox (bubblewrap/landlock) is the real long-term control.
agy gate: agy itself lets a plain accept-edits run write anywhere by absolute path, so every agy run
(plain and --agent; not --yolo) gets a PreToolUse hook in <wt>/.agents/hooks.json (never committed):
scripts/agy-gate.py allows view_file, list_dir, grep_search, find_by_name and (not under --review)
write_to_file, edit_file, replace_file_content on absolute or file:/// paths that resolve inside the
worktree, outside any .git or .agents-style component (.gemini too), never the root AGENTS.md or GEMINI.md; plain runs also get run_command for read-only
commands from the runner allowlist (git status/diff/log/show, ls, pwd, echo, wc, cat of source paths; no
shell syntax, paths inside the worktree). No test runner: it would run worker-written code past the gate. Everything else is denied (MCP, browser, web),
and every decision is logged into task/gate.log; denials land in denied_actions (reads of .git or .agents are
denied quietly: counted in quiet_denials, a warning above 3). agy runs a hook that crashes or prints nothing as
an allow, so before the commit the tool names in agy's transcript of this run are matched one by one against
the gate log: a mismatch ("gate hook inactive"), an unreadable transcript ("gate check unavailable") or a
resume that answered for another conversation is NOT ok and not committed. A base that tracks anything under
.agents/.agent/_agents/_agent/.gemini is refused, and so is a launch (start after --setup, resume) while the worktree
has any such entry besides the wrapper's own overlay, or a symlink among them.
The gate's schema (tool names, argument keys, transcript format) was probed on agy 1.4.2 (AGY_PROBED): another
agy version is refused unless AGY_TASK_ALLOW_UNPROBED=1. Re-probe before bumping it: in a scratch repo, run one
plain and one --agent task that reads, edits and searches; compare the tool names and argument keys in
~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/<conversation>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl and the gate log
with agy-gate.py's schema, and add only file tools whose path keys are known.

Invoked as opencode-task (a symlink) it drives `opencode run`: branches opencode/<slug>, tasks under
$OPENCODE_TASK_DIR (default ~/.opencode-tasks). A per-run config overlay (OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT, this
process only) allows edits (file tools denied outside the worktree), limits the shell to test/build runners and read-only git, and turns off
subagents; the user's own OpenCode config is untouched. --yolo lifts the shell limit (not sandboxed).
Circuit breaker (opencode): the JSON stream is watched while the worker runs. At --max-denied denied
commands (a worker that keeps trying shell workarounds) or --max-tool-errors failed tool calls its process
group is killed, its edits are kept and committed, and result.json gets ok false, a "stopped: ..." warning
and "stopped_by": "max-denied" | "max-tool-errors" (also "timeout" on a timeout). Resume a
stopped worker at most once (only if its edits are worth keeping); then take the task over. 0 disables a limit; agy is not watched.
--effort sets the model variant (opencode: "provider/model#effort"). Left out, a model gets its default
from a small table (currently empty); a model not in the table gets no effort suffix, since a variant
a model lacks fails the whole run (muse rejects `max`). --effort "" forces none. Resume reuses the model and effort of start.

A worker can run as a named specialist with --agent NAME (start only, rejected on resume, which reuses it). On opencode
without --model the worker uses the agent's own `model:` when it is on the worker allowlist, else the lane default
(with a stderr notice); --model always wins and must be on the allowlist. A headless note (no browser or MCP here) is prepended to the prompt.
--agent is rejected for the lead-dev-hybrid orchestrator and for unknown agents.
opencode: `--agent NAME` instead of `--agent build`; the sandbox overlay is also applied under
`agent.NAME.permission`, so the agent's own permission block (e.g. bash '*': allow) cannot widen it.
Agents: opencode/agents/NAME.md ($SWARMKIT_OPENCODE_AGENTS_DIR in tests).
agy: `--agent NAME` plus .agents/agents/NAME/agent.md in the worktree (never committed): the plugin agent
with an explicit tool list (file tools only, read-only under --review, no shell or MCP), next to the gate
hook above (no shell for --agent). An agent whose frontmatter already sets tools, inheritMcp, hooks, plugins
or commandExecutionPolicy is refused, on start and again on resume. --yolo adds the shell and drops the hook.
Agents: antigravity/plugins/swarmkit/agents/NAME.md ($SWARMKIT_AGY_AGENTS_DIR in tests).

start and resume print one banner line to stderr before the worker launches (slug, model, effort, base, log);
the log is written live, and list shows model, elapsed time or wall seconds and (opencode) the live denied count.

$SWARMKIT_DISPATCH_LOG=FILE: JSON lines with only allowlisted fields. At launch: ts, event "start", cli, slug,
model, effort, agent. Per finished task: ts, event "finish", cli, slug, model, agent, ok, denied (count), tokens (total or
null), wall_s and stopped_by (null | max-denied | max-tool-errors | timeout).

The running-task limit is shared: agy and opencode tasks of all repos together never exceed it
(the limit itself is read from the invoked backend's *_TASK_MAX). list and clean stay per repo.
"""
import argparse, fcntl, functools, hashlib, json, os, re, shlex, shutil, signal, stat, subprocess, sys, threading, time
from pathlib import Path

# opencode-task is a symlink to this file; the name picks the backend
PROG = "opencode-task" if Path(sys.argv[0]).name == "opencode-task" else "agy-task"


def seconds(s):
    return int(s[:-1]) * {"s": 1, "m": 60, "h": 3600}[s[-1]] if s[-1] in "smh" else int(s)


def agy_cmd(task, prompt, a, resume_id):
    agent = getattr(a, "agent", None)
    agy_overlay(task, a, agent)
    if agent:
        prompt = HEADLESS_NOTE + "\n\n" + prompt
    cmd = ["agy", "-p", prompt, "--output-format", "json", "--mode", "accept-edits",
           "--print-timeout", f"{seconds(a.timeout)}s"] + (["--agent", agent] if agent else [])
    if resume_id:
        cmd += ["--conversation", resume_id]
    else:
        cmd += ["--model", a.model] + (["--effort", a.effort] if a.effort else [])
    if a.yolo:
        cmd.append("--dangerously-skip-permissions")
        print("agy-task: --yolo, agy is unsandboxed", file=sys.stderr)
    return cmd


def agy_parse(out, err):
    try:
        res = json.loads(out)
    except ValueError:
        res = {}
    return {"done": res.get("status") == "SUCCESS", "conversation_id": res.get("conversation_id"),
            "usage": res.get("usage"), "response": res.get("response", ""),
            "denied": [d.get("display_name", d.get("action")) for d in res.get("denied_actions", [])],
            # agy exits 0 with partial output when its own timeout hits
            "timed_out": bool(re.search(r"print timeout", err))}


# Effort per model when --effort is not given. Not listed: no effort (a variant the model lacks is an error).
EFFORT_DEFAULTS = {}


def remembered_opts(task, a, resume_id):
    """Model, effort and agent of the first run: opencode forgets them on resume."""
    f = task / "opts.json"
    if resume_id:
        return json.loads(f.read_text()) if f.exists() else {}
    o = {"model": a.model, "effort": a.effort, "agent": getattr(a, "agent", None),
         "gitdir": json.loads(f.read_text()).get("gitdir") if f.exists() else None}  # recorded by start
    f.write_text(json.dumps(o))
    return o


# Applied only to the delegated run (OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT), so the user's own OpenCode config is
# untouched: edits allowed, the shell limited to common test/build runners and read-only git, no subagents,
# no file tool outside the worktree (external_directory; the shell is limited by its allowlist instead).
# A guard against accidents, not a sandbox: a test runner executes code the worker can write itself.
RUNNERS = ("npm test", "npm run test", "npm run lint", "npm run build", "npm run typecheck", "pnpm test",
           "pnpm run test", "pnpm run lint", "pnpm run build", "yarn test", "yarn lint", "yarn build",
           "bun test", "python3 -m pytest", "python -m pytest", "pytest", "python3 -m unittest",
           "python -m unittest", "go test", "go vet", "cargo test", "cargo check", "make test",
           "node --test", "node test.js", "node --version", "git status", "git diff", "git log", "git show")
# Patterns that need their own shape (the loop below only adds "<cmd>" and "<cmd> *"): plain-node and
# plain-python test files, test files in a subdirectory too (not `python3 *`: that runs arbitrary code), and the read-only commands models
# reach for to look around (ls, pwd, echo, wc for line counts, cat of source and test paths only, so
# `cat .env` stays denied). Not `cd`: the worker already starts in the worktree, and
# `cd <elsewhere> && npm test` would test a different checkout.
# Fixed prefixes only, never a leading wildcard: `*` also matches flags such as `-e`, so `node */test/*`
# would allow `node -e "<code>" x/test/y`. Add one entry per extra project directory if needed.
RUNNER_GLOBS = ("node test/*", "node tests/*", "node __tests__/*", "node site/test/*", "node site/tests/*",
                "python3 test/*", "python3 tests/*",
                "pwd", "ls", "ls *", "echo *", "wc *",
                "cat src/*", "cat test/*", "cat tests/*", "cat package.json", "cat README.md")
OPENCODE_OVERLAY = {
    "permission": {
        # opencode matches the worktree-relative path, `*` also crosses `/`, and the last matching rule wins
        "edit": {"*": "allow", **{g: "deny" for g in (".git", ".git/*", "**/.git", "**/.git/*")}},
        "webfetch": "deny", "task": "deny", "external_directory": "deny",
        "bash": {"*": "deny", **{p: "allow" for c in RUNNERS for p in (c, c + " *")},
                 **{g: "allow" for g in RUNNER_GLOBS},
                 # after the allows (last match wins): read-only git must not write files, read outside the
                 # worktree or run an external diff. `*` also matches `=`, so `--output=x` is covered.
                 # git takes any unique prefix of an option, 4 characters suffice: --ou(tput), --no-i(ndex), --ext(-diff)
                 **{g: "deny" for g in ("git * --ou*", "git * --no-i*", "git * --ext*")}},
    },
}


def agents_dir():
    d = os.environ.get("SWARMKIT_OPENCODE_AGENTS_DIR")
    return Path(d) if d else Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "opencode" / "agents"


def agent_model(agent):
    """The `model:` value of the agent's frontmatter, quotes stripped; "" if it has none."""
    for line in (agents_dir() / f"{agent}.md").read_text().split("\n---", 1)[0].splitlines():
        m = re.match(r"model:\s*(.*?)\s*$", line)
        if m:
            return m.group(1).strip("'\"")
    return ""


def agent_edits_git(agent):
    """True if the agent's frontmatter `edit:` map (block or inline form) has a non-deny rule that names .git
    (`.git/hooks/*`, `.gi?`) or matches a .git path as a whole (`**`; opencode's `*` crosses `/`): merged with
    the overlay, it would land after the .git deny and win. `*` is the overlay's own first key, so it keeps its
    place. `**/test/**` passes; a nested .git it could write is caught after the run (nested_gits)."""
    def glob(k):
        return re.compile(re.escape(k).replace(r"\*", ".*").replace(r"\?", "."))
    def risky(entry):
        m = re.match(r"\s*(['\"]?)(.*?)\1\s*:\s*['\"]?(\w*)", entry)
        if not m or m.group(3) == "deny" or m.group(2) == "*":
            return False
        k = m.group(2)
        return any(glob(k).fullmatch(x) for x in (".git", ".git/config", ".git/hooks/x", "x/.git", "x/.git/config")) \
            or any(glob(c).fullmatch(".git") for c in k.split("/") if not re.fullmatch(r"\*+", c))
    lines = (agents_dir() / f"{agent}.md").read_text().split("\n---", 1)[0].splitlines()
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        m = re.match(r"(\s*)edit:\s*(.*)$", line)
        if not m:
            continue
        if m.group(2).startswith("{"):
            if any(risky(e) for e in m.group(2).strip("{} ").split(",")):
                return True
            continue
        for sub in lines[i + 1:]:
            if len(sub) - len(sub.lstrip()) <= len(m.group(1)):
                break
            if risky(sub):
                return True
    return False


HEADLESS_NOTE = ("Headless worker: there is no browser or MCP here, so skip Playwright/screenshot steps;"
                 " the orchestrator verifies visually.")


def agy_agents_dir():
    d = os.environ.get("SWARMKIT_AGY_AGENTS_DIR")
    return Path(d) if d else Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "antigravity" / "plugins" / "swarmkit" / "agents"


# Every agy run (plain and --agent) gets a PreToolUse hook in the worktree's .agents/hooks.json, a workspace
# customization agy loads for plain runs too: agy-gate.py allows the file tools on worktree paths only, and
# on plain runs run_command for read-only commands (AGY_SHELL); everything else (MCP, browser, other paths,
# .git, .agents) is denied. A named agy agent also gets only the tools its frontmatter lists, and headless agy
# auto-denies even reads under it, so --agent adds the agent with an explicit tool list (no run_command, no
# MCP) next to the hook. The commit skips both; the user's agy settings stay untouched.
AGY_TOOLS = ("view_file", "list_dir", "grep_search", "find_by_name")
AGY_EDIT_TOOLS = ("write_to_file", "edit_file", "replace_file_content")
AGY_ROOTS = (".agents", ".agent", "_agents", "_agent", ".gemini")  # agy's customization roots; the gate denies them
AGY_AGENT_KEYS = ("tools", "inheritMcp", "hooks", "plugins", "commandExecutionPolicy")  # the overlay sets these
# A plain run's shell: the read-only part of the runner allowlist. No test runner: it runs code the worker can
# write, which would walk around the gate (plain agy had no shell at all before the gate).
AGY_SHELL = [p for c in RUNNERS if c.startswith("git ") for p in (c, c + " *")] + \
            [g for g in RUNNER_GLOBS if not g.startswith(("node ", "python3 "))]


def agy_agent_problem(agent):
    """Why NAME cannot run as an agy worker, or None (checked on start and again on resume)."""
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*", agent or ""):
        return f"invalid agent name: {agent}"
    if agent == "lead-dev-hybrid":
        return "orchestrators cannot run as workers: lead-dev-hybrid"
    f = agy_agents_dir() / f"{agent}.md"
    if not f.is_file() or f.is_symlink():
        return f"unknown Antigravity agent: {agent}"
    parts = f.read_text().split("---\n", 2)
    if len(parts) != 3 or parts[0]:
        return f"agent {agent} has no frontmatter"
    keys = [k for k in AGY_AGENT_KEYS if re.search(rf"^\s*['\"]?{k}['\"]?\s*:", parts[1], re.M | re.I)]
    if keys:
        return f"agent {agent} sets {', '.join(keys)} in its frontmatter; the worker sandbox sets those itself"
    return None


AGY_PROBED = "1.4.2"  # the agy version the gate schema and transcript check were probed on


def refuse(task, msg):
    (task / "pid").unlink(missing_ok=True)
    print(f"{PROG}: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)


def write_nofollow(path, text):
    """Create or truncate a regular file, never through a symlink (or a FIFO: O_NONBLOCK fails instead of hanging)."""
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, 0o644)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(f.fileno()).st_mode):
            raise OSError(f"{path} is not a regular file")
        f.write(text)


def agy_roots_problem(wt, agent):
    """Why agy must not launch in WT, or None: agy loads hooks, agents and rules from .agents-style dirs, so the
    only entries allowed there are the overlay's own (real dirs and files, no symlinks)."""
    own = {".agents": "d", ".agents/hooks.json": "f"}
    if agent:
        own.update({".agents/agents": "d", f".agents/agents/{agent}": "d", f".agents/agents/{agent}/agent.md": "f"})
    for d, dirs, files in os.walk(wt):  # followlinks=False: a symlinked dir is listed, not entered
        if d == str(wt):
            dirs[:] = [n for n in dirs if n != ".git"]
        for n in dirs + files:
            f = os.path.join(d, n)
            r = os.path.relpath(f, wt)
            if not {c.lower() for c in r.split(os.sep)} & set(AGY_ROOTS):
                continue
            kind = "l" if os.path.islink(f) else "d" if os.path.isdir(f) else "f" if os.path.isfile(f) else "o"
            if own.get(r) != kind:
                return f"{r} is in an agy customization dir ({'a symlink' if kind == 'l' else 'not the overlay'})"
    return None


def agy_overlay(task, a, agent):
    wt = task / "worktree"
    bad = agy_roots_problem(wt, agent)  # every launch: --setup or an earlier run could have planted one
    if bad:
        refuse(task, f"refusing to launch agy: {bad}; remove it from {wt} or clean the task")
    hooks, overlay = wt / ".agents" / "hooks.json", [".agents/hooks.json"]
    if agent:
        _, fm, body = (agy_agents_dir() / f"{agent}.md").read_text().split("---\n", 2)
        tools = AGY_TOOLS + (() if a.review else AGY_EDIT_TOOLS) + (("run_command",) if a.yolo else ())
        fm = fm.rstrip("\n") + "\ninheritMcp: false\ntools:\n" + "".join(f"  - {t}\n" for t in tools)
        d = wt / ".agents" / "agents" / agent
        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        write_nofollow(d / "agent.md", f"---\n{fm}---\n{body}")
        overlay.append(f".agents/agents/{agent}")
    (task / "gate.log").unlink(missing_ok=True)  # this run's gate decisions (the gate creates it, O_NOFOLLOW)
    if a.yolo:  # unsandboxed: no gate
        hooks.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    else:
        hooks.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        shell = [] if agent else AGY_SHELL
        write_nofollow(task / "gate.json", json.dumps({"root": str(wt), "log": str(task / "gate.log"),
                                                       "edit": not a.review, "shell": shell}))
        gate = ["python3", "-I", str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "agy-gate.py"), str(task / "gate.json")]
        write_nofollow(hooks, json.dumps({"swarmkit-worktree-gate": {"PreToolUse": [
            {"matcher": "*", "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": shlex.join(gate), "timeout": 10}]}]}}, indent=1))
    write_nofollow(task / "overlay", "\n".join(overlay))


def gate_name(s):
    """A tool name as agy-gate.py logs it."""
    return re.sub(r"[\x00-\x1f\x7f-\x9f\u2028\u2029]", "?", str(s))[:300]


def agy_tool_calls(conv):
    """The tool names agy's transcript of this conversation records, in order, or None if it cannot be read."""
    if not conv or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f-]{8,64}", str(conv)):
        return None
    brain = Path(os.environ.get("SWARMKIT_AGY_BRAIN_DIR", Path.home() / ".gemini" / "antigravity-cli" / "brain"))
    names = []
    try:
        for line in read_nofollow(brain / conv / ".system_generated" / "logs" / "transcript_full.jsonl").splitlines():
            try:  # an unreadable line drops its calls: a shorter list never matches the gate log
                names += [gate_name(c.get("name")) for c in json.loads(line).get("tool_calls") or []]
            except (ValueError, AttributeError, TypeError):
                pass
    except OSError:
        return None
    return names


def read_nofollow(path):
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    with os.fdopen(fd, errors="replace") as f:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(f.fileno()).st_mode):
            raise OSError(f"{path} is not a regular file")
        return f.read()


def opencode_cmd(task, prompt, a, resume_id):
    o = remembered_opts(task, a, resume_id)
    agent = o.get("agent")
    if agent:
        prompt = HEADLESS_NOTE + "\n\n" + prompt
    if a.yolo:
        print("opencode-task: --yolo, the shell is unrestricted and unsandboxed", file=sys.stderr)
    # --standalone: a private server started with our env (and so the overlay). The shared background
    # service would apply the user's own config.
    cmd = ["opencode", "run", "--standalone", "--format", "json", "--agent", agent or "build",
           "--title", f"delegate: {task.name}"] + (["-s", resume_id] if resume_id else [])
    if o.get("model"):
        cmd += ["-m", o["model"] + (f"#{o['effort']}" if o.get("effort") else "")]
    return cmd + ["--", prompt]


def opencode_env(a, wt):
    perm = dict(OPENCODE_OVERLAY["permission"])
    if a.yolo:
        perm["bash"] = "allow"
    if a.review:  # a review answers in text and must not edit
        perm["edit"] = "deny"
    cfg = {"permission": perm}
    agent = getattr(a, "agent", None)
    if agent:
        if agent_edits_git(agent):
            sys.exit(f"{PROG}: agent {agent} has an edit rule for .git; it cannot run as a worker")
        cfg["agent"] = {agent: {"permission": perm}}
    # opencode takes its project directory from $PWD, not the real cwd: without this it edits the
    # checkout agy-task was started from instead of the worktree.
    return {**os.environ, "PWD": str(wt), "OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT": json.dumps(cfg)}


DENIED = re.compile(r"rule which prevents|permission|rejected", re.I)


def tool_failure(line):
    """(failed, denied) for one JSON line: a tool call that errored, and whether a permission rule refused it."""
    try:
        e = json.loads(line)
    except ValueError:
        return False, False
    st = (e.get("part") or {}).get("state") or {}
    if e.get("type") != "tool_use" or st.get("status") != "error":
        return False, False
    return True, bool(DENIED.search(str(st.get("error", ""))))


def opencode_parse(out, err):
    r = {"done": False, "conversation_id": None, "usage": None, "response": "", "denied": [],
         "timed_out": False}
    failed, usage = False, {}  # failed: an error with no finished step after it (retries can recover)
    for line in out.splitlines():
        try:
            e = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        t, part = e.get("type"), e.get("part") or {}
        r["conversation_id"] = r["conversation_id"] or e.get("sessionID")
        if t == "error":
            failed = True
        elif t == "text" and part.get("text", "").strip():
            r["response"] = part["text"]
        elif t == "step_finish":
            r["done"], failed = True, False
            tok = part.get("tokens") or {}
            for k in ("input", "output", "reasoning"):
                usage[k] = usage.get(k, 0) + tok.get(k, 0)
            usage["cache_read"] = usage.get("cache_read", 0) + (tok.get("cache") or {}).get("read", 0)
        elif t == "tool_use":
            st = part.get("state") or {}
            if tool_failure(line)[1]:
                inp = st.get("input") or {}
                r["denied"].append(inp.get("command") or part.get("tool", "tool"))
    r["done"] = r["done"] and not failed
    r["usage"] = usage or None
    return r


BACKENDS = {
    "agy-task": {"cli": "agy", "env": "AGY_TASK", "home": ".agy-tasks",
                 "model": "gemini-3.8-flash-high", "cmd": agy_cmd, "parse": agy_parse, "grace": 30,
                 "allowed": ("gemini-3.8-flash-high", "gemini-3.8-flash-medium", "gemini-3.8-flash-low")},
    "opencode-task": {"cli": "opencode", "env": "OPENCODE_TASK", "home": ".opencode-tasks",
                      "model": "opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor", "cmd": opencode_cmd,
                      "parse": opencode_parse, "grace": 0, "proc_env": opencode_env, "watch": tool_failure,
                      "allowed": ("opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash", "opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash",
                                  "opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-pro", "opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor",
                                  # TODO: remove beam-free when its free period ends
                                  "opencode-go/beam-free")},
}
BACKEND = BACKENDS[PROG]
CLI = BACKEND["cli"]


def alive(pidfile):
    try:
        pid = int(pidfile.read_text())
        os.kill(pid, 0)
        cmdline = Path(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline").read_bytes()
        return any(name.encode() in cmdline for name in BACKENDS)  # not a recycled pid
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False


def sh(*cmd, cwd=None, check=True):
    p = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, text=True, capture_output=True)
    if check and p.returncode:
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {' '.join(cmd[:3])} failed: {p.stderr.strip() or p.stdout.strip()}")
    return p.stdout.strip()


# Repository-location variables from our caller's environment must not redirect the pinned calls.
GIT_LOCATION_ENV = ("GIT_INDEX_FILE", "GIT_COMMON_DIR", "GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY", "GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES")


def git_common(repo):
    """The main repo's git common dir (main-repo-owned: the pin is checked against it)."""
    return Path(os.path.realpath(sh("git", "-C", str(repo), "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir")))


def check_pin(p):
    """None if the pinned gitdir is still the main repo's own record of this worktree, else what is wrong."""
    wt, g, common = p["wt"], Path(p["gitdir"]), p["common"]
    if os.path.realpath(wt) != str(wt) or wt.is_symlink() or not wt.is_dir():
        return f"{wt} is not a real directory (a symlink or moved)"
    if g.parent != common / "worktrees" or os.path.realpath(g) != str(g) or not g.is_dir():
        return f"recorded gitdir {g} is not an entry of {common / 'worktrees'}"
    try:
        if (g / "gitdir").read_text().strip() != str(wt / ".git"):
            return f"{g / 'gitdir'} does not point at {wt / '.git'}"
        if os.path.realpath(g / (g / "commondir").read_text().strip()) != str(common):
            return f"{g / 'commondir'} does not point at {common}"
    except OSError as e:
        return f"cannot read the worktree record: {e}"
    return None


def pin(task, repo):
    """Read the recorded gitdir once and check it; every wt_git call of this run uses only what this returns."""
    wt, f = task / "worktree", task / "opts.json"
    gitdir = json.loads(f.read_text()).get("gitdir") if f.exists() else None
    if not gitdir:
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {task.name} has no recorded gitdir (started before git isolation); "
                 f"inspect {wt} by hand, then clean it with --force")
    base = (task / "base").read_text().strip() if (task / "base").exists() else ""
    p = {"wt": wt, "gitdir": gitdir, "common": git_common(repo), "base": base,
         "dotgit": f"gitdir: {gitdir}\n".encode()}
    bad = check_pin(p) or (None if re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40,64}", base) else f"bad base commit {base!r}") \
        or (None if (task / "dotgit").exists() and (task / "dotgit").read_bytes() == p["dotgit"]
            else f"{task / 'dotgit'} does not match the recorded gitdir")
    if bad:
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {task.name}: {bad}; inspect it by hand, then clean it with --force")
    return p


@functools.cache
def git_version():
    return tuple(int(x) for x in re.findall(r"\d+", sh("git", "--version"))[:2])


def wt_git(p, *args, check=True):
    """git in a task worktree, pinned to the checked gitdir. Never through <wt>/.git: the worker can rewrite
    it to point at a gitdir whose config or hooks run commands on the host."""
    bad = check_pin(p)  # before every call: a changed worktree record could reroute GIT_DIR's commondir
    if bad:
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: refusing git in {p['wt']}: {bad}")
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in GIT_LOCATION_ENV}
    env.update(GIT_DIR=p["gitdir"], GIT_WORK_TREE=str(p["wt"]), GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM="1")
    # attributes from the base commit, not the worktree (git 2.40+): a worker-written .gitattributes picks no filter
    attr = [f"--attr-source={p['base']}"] if git_version() >= (2, 40) else []
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "--no-pager", *attr, "-c", "core.fsmonitor=false", "-c", "core.hooksPath=/dev/null",
                        "-c", "gc.auto=0", "-c", "maintenance.auto=false", *args],
                       cwd=p["wt"], env=env, text=True, capture_output=True)
    if check and r.returncode:
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: git {' '.join(args[:2])} failed: {r.stderr.strip() or r.stdout.strip()}")
    return r.stdout.strip()


def dotgit_ok(p):
    f = p["wt"] / ".git"
    return not f.is_symlink() and f.is_file() and f.read_bytes() == p["dotgit"]


def restore_dotgit(p):
    """Put back <wt>/.git as derived from the pinned gitdir; True if the worker had changed it (file, dir or symlink)."""
    if dotgit_ok(p):
        return False
    f = p["wt"] / ".git"
    if f.is_dir() and not f.is_symlink():
        shutil.rmtree(f)
    elif f.is_symlink() or f.exists():
        f.unlink()
    fd = os.open(f, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o644)  # never through a new symlink
    with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as w:
        w.write(p["dotgit"])
    return True


def nested_gits(wt):
    """Each entry named .git (any case) below the worktree root, and the root .gitmodules, with a content
    signature: a nested repo's own config or a submodule entry would make git run what the worker planted."""
    def sig(path):  # regular files only: reading a planted FIFO would hang the wrapper
        try:
            if os.path.islink(path):
                return "link:" + os.readlink(path)
            if os.path.isdir(path):
                return "dir:" + "".join(hashlib.sha1(Path(path, n).read_bytes()).hexdigest() if Path(path, n).is_file()
                                        else "-" for n in ("config", "HEAD", "commondir", "gitdir"))
            return "file:" + hashlib.sha1(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest() if os.path.isfile(path) else "other"
        except OSError as e:
            return f"unreadable: {e}"
    found = {}
    for d, dirs, files in os.walk(wt):  # followlinks=False: a symlinked dir is listed, not entered
        for n in dirs + files:
            if n.lower() == ".git" and not (d == str(wt) and n == ".git"):
                found[os.path.relpath(os.path.join(d, n), wt)] = sig(os.path.join(d, n))
        dirs[:] = [n for n in dirs if n.lower() != ".git"]
    if os.path.lexists(wt / ".gitmodules"):
        found[".gitmodules"] = sig(str(wt / ".gitmodules"))
    return found


def git_meta(p):
    """Hash of the git metadata a worker could plant commands in: the main repo's config, hooks, info/, this
    worktree's own record (HEAD too: pointed at main's branch, our commit would land there) and the user's
    global git config and attributes."""
    c, g, h = p["common"], Path(p["gitdir"]), hashlib.sha1()
    xdg = Path(os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") or Path.home() / ".config") / "git"
    for f in [c / "config", c / "config.worktree", g / "commondir", g / "gitdir", g / "config.worktree", g / "HEAD",
              Path.home() / ".gitconfig", xdg / "config", xdg / "attributes",
              *[x for d in (c / "hooks", c / "info") for x in ([d, *sorted(d.rglob("*"))] if d.is_dir() else [d])]]:
        try:
            v = (b"link:" + os.readlink(f).encode() if f.is_symlink() else f.read_bytes() if f.is_file()
                 else b"dir" if f.is_dir() else b"other" if os.path.lexists(f) else b"none")
        except OSError as e:
            v = str(e).encode()
        h.update(str(f).encode() + b"\0" + v + b"\0")
    return h.hexdigest()


def spec(task):
    """Pathspec for the worktree: everything except what --setup created and the agy --agent overlay."""
    fs = [task / "setup-artifacts", task / "overlay"]
    return ["--", ".", *[f":(exclude){x}" for f in fs if f.exists() for x in f.read_text().split("\n") if x]]


def main_state(repo):
    """Changed and untracked paths of the main checkout, with a content hash for each."""
    out = subprocess.run(["git", "-c", "core.fsmonitor=false", "status", "--porcelain", "-uall", "-z"], cwd=repo, text=True,
                         capture_output=True).stdout  # not sh(): stripping would eat the status column
    state, fields = {}, iter(out.split("\0"))
    for entry in fields:
        if not entry:
            continue
        if entry[0] in "RC":  # a rename or copy is followed by its source path
            next(fields, None)
        f = repo / entry[3:]
        state[entry[3:]] = hashlib.sha1(f.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if f.is_file() else entry[:2]
    return state


def dispatch_log(event, slug, model, **fields):
    """Append one allowlisted line per event to $SWARMKIT_DISPATCH_LOG: no prompt, path or command."""
    path = os.environ.get("SWARMKIT_DISPATCH_LOG")
    if not path:
        return
    line = {"ts": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()), "event": event, "cli": CLI, "slug": slug,
            "model": model, **fields}
    try:
        with open(path, "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(line) + "\n")
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"{PROG}: WARNING: dispatch log not written: {e}", file=sys.stderr)


def list_extra(d, r, running):
    """Model, elapsed (running) or wall seconds (finished) and the live denied count, as a column prefix."""
    try:
        o = json.loads((d / "opts.json").read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        o = {}
    model = (r.get("model") or o.get("model") or "?").removeprefix("opencode-go/")  # other providers stay visible
    if running:
        n = int(time.time() - (d / "pid").stat().st_mtime)
        t = f"{n // 3600}h{n % 3600 // 60:02}m" if n >= 3600 else f"{n // 60}m{n % 60:02}s"
    else:
        t = f"{r['wall_s']}s" if "wall_s" in r else "-"
    denied = ""
    if running and CLI == "opencode":  # the log is written live
        try:
            n = sum(tool_failure(line)[1] for line in (d / "opencode.log").read_text().splitlines())
        except OSError:
            n = 0
        denied = f"denied {n} "
    elif r.get("denied_actions"):
        denied = f"denied {len(r['denied_actions'])} "
    return f"{model:27.27} {t:>6} {denied}"


def banner(task, o, resume_id):
    """One stderr line when a worker launches, so the owner can see which model runs where."""
    home = str(Path.home())
    log = str(task / f"{CLI}.log")
    log = "~" + log[len(home):] if log.startswith(home + "/") else log
    base = (task / "base").read_text().strip()[:7]
    print(f"{PROG} \u25b6 {task.name} \u00b7 model {o.get('model') or 'unknown'} \u00b7 effort {o.get('effort') or 'none'}"
          f" \u00b7 base {base} \u00b7 log {log}" + (" \u00b7 resume" if resume_id else ""), file=sys.stderr)


def run_task(task, prompt, a, repo, resume_id=None, warnings=()):
    wt, t0 = task / "worktree", time.monotonic()
    (task / "pid").write_text(str(os.getpid()))
    o = remembered_opts(task, a, resume_id)
    if o.get("agent"):
        a.agent = o["agent"]
    pinned = pin(task, repo)  # read and checked once, before the worker runs; this run uses only this
    meta_before = git_meta(pinned)
    nf = task / "nested-git"  # what --setup left (e.g. a submodule); anything else is the worker's
    nested_before = json.loads(nf.read_text()) if nf.exists() else {}
    gated = CLI == "agy" and not a.yolo
    calls_before = (agy_tool_calls(resume_id) if resume_id else []) if gated else None
    cmd = BACKEND["cmd"](task, prompt, a, resume_id)
    banner(task, o, resume_id)
    dispatch_log("start", task.name, o.get("model"), effort=o.get("effort") or None, agent=o.get("agent"))
    logf = open(task / f"{CLI}.log", "w")  # live, so `tail -f` and `list` work; rewritten in order at the end
    main_before = main_state(repo)
    # Own process group so a SIGTERM/SIGINT to us (or a timeout) takes the agent and its tools down too.
    env = BACKEND["proc_env"](a, wt) if "proc_env" in BACKEND else None
    p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, cwd=wt, env=env, text=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True,
                         stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
    interrupted, stopped, killer, counts, bufs = [], [], [], {"failed": 0, "denied": 0}, {"out": [], "err": []}

    def killpg(sig):
        try:
            os.killpg(p.pid, sig)
        except OSError:
            pass
    def stop(signum=None, frame=None):
        interrupted.append(signum or "timeout")
        killpg(signal.SIGTERM)
    def watch(line):  # circuit breaker: a worker stuck retrying denied or broken tool calls burns quota for nothing
        if stopped:  # already killed; the rest of the buffered output only goes to the log
            return
        failed, denied = BACKEND["watch"](line)
        counts["failed"] += failed
        counts["denied"] += denied
        why = ("max-denied" if a.max_denied and counts["denied"] >= a.max_denied else
               "max-tool-errors" if a.max_tool_errors and counts["failed"] >= a.max_tool_errors else None)
        if why and not stopped:
            stopped.append(why)
            killpg(signal.SIGTERM)
            killer.append(threading.Timer(10, killpg, (signal.SIGKILL,)))  # if SIGTERM is ignored
            killer[0].start()
    def pump(stream, buf, on_line=None):  # drain a pipe while the agent runs, so we can react mid-run
        for line in stream:
            buf.append(line)
            logf.write(line)
            logf.flush()
            if on_line:
                on_line(line)
    readers = [threading.Thread(target=pump, args=(p.stdout, bufs["out"], watch if "watch" in BACKEND else None), daemon=True),
               threading.Thread(target=pump, args=(p.stderr, bufs["err"]), daemon=True)]
    for t in readers:
        t.start()
    old = [signal.signal(sig, stop) for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT)]
    try:
        p.wait(timeout=seconds(a.timeout) + BACKEND["grace"])
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        stop()
        try:  # SIGTERM was sent; escalate if the agent or a tool ignores it
            p.wait(timeout=10)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            killpg(signal.SIGKILL)
            p.wait(timeout=10)
    finally:
        for sig, h in zip((signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT), old):
            signal.signal(sig, h)
    for k in killer:
        k.cancel()
    for t in readers:  # EOF follows the exit unless a straggler in the group still holds the pipe
        t.join(5)
    if interrupted or stopped or any(t.is_alive() for t in readers):
        killpg(signal.SIGKILL)  # stragglers from the process group
        for t in readers:
            t.join(5)
    out, err = "".join(bufs["out"]), "".join(bufs["err"])
    code = p.returncode
    (task / "pid").unlink(missing_ok=True)
    logf.close()
    (task / f"{CLI}.log").write_text(f"{err}\n{out}")
    res = BACKEND["parse"](out, err)
    gate_log = []
    if gated:  # agy-gate.py's decisions; agy does not report its denials
        try:
            gate_log = [x for x in read_nofollow(task / "gate.log").splitlines() if x]
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
        except OSError as e:
            gate_log = [f"deny ? gate log unreadable: {e}"]
        res["denied"] += [x.split(" ", 1)[1] for x in gate_log if x.startswith("deny ")]
    warnings = list(warnings)
    # The main repo's git metadata first: if it changed, run no git at all (not even main_state's status).
    meta = check_pin(pinned) or ("" if git_meta(pinned) == meta_before else "config, hooks, info/ or worktree record")
    if meta:
        warnings.append(f"git metadata changed during the run ({meta}): nothing was auto-committed or inspected;"
                        f" check {pinned['common']} before running git there")
    else:
        after = main_state(repo)
        moved = sorted(k for k in main_before.keys() | after.keys() if main_before.get(k) != after.get(k))
        if moved:  # advisory: you may have edited or merged there yourself meanwhile
            warnings.append(f"main checkout changed during the run, not by you? {', '.join(moved[:5])}")
    if interrupted:
        warnings.append(f"interrupted: {CLI} was stopped before it finished")
    if res["timed_out"]:
        warnings.append("timed out: the response and edits may be incomplete")
    if stopped:
        n = counts["denied"] if stopped[0] == "max-denied" else counts["failed"]
        warnings.append(f"stopped: {n} {'denied commands' if stopped[0] == 'max-denied' else 'failed tool calls'}"
                        f" ({CLI} was killed; its edits are kept, inspect the diff)")
    # It may have pointed git at a gitdir it planted: restore .git, commit nothing, let the owner look.
    blocked = []
    moved_wt = check_pin(pinned)  # the worktree path or its record changed: touch nothing in there
    if moved_wt:
        blocked.append(f"worker modified .git or the worktree path ({moved_wt}): left as it is")
    else:
        try:
            if restore_dotgit(pinned):
                blocked.append("worker modified .git: restored it")
        except OSError as e:
            blocked.append(f"worker modified .git and it could not be restored ({e})")
        nested_after = nested_gits(wt)
        for k in sorted(k for k in nested_before.keys() | nested_after.keys() if nested_before.get(k) != nested_after.get(k)):
            blocked.append("worker changed .gitmodules" if k == ".gitmodules" else f"worker created a nested .git at {k}")
        if not meta:  # symbolic-ref follows symref chains: a branch ref turned into a symref is caught too
            head = wt_git(pinned, "symbolic-ref", "-q", "HEAD", check=False)
            if head != f"refs/heads/{CLI}/{task.name}":
                blocked.append(f"worker moved HEAD to {head or 'a detached commit'}")
    quiet = sum(x.startswith("deny-quiet ") for x in gate_log)
    if gated:  # agy runs a hook that crashed or printed nothing as if it allowed (fails open): catch that before the commit
        calls = agy_tool_calls(res["conversation_id"])
        seen = [(x.split(" ") + [""])[1] for x in gate_log]  # every decision, deny-quiet too: the transcript has those calls
        new = calls[len(calls_before):] if calls is not None and calls_before is not None else None
        if resume_id and res["conversation_id"] != resume_id:
            blocked.append(f"gate check failed: agy answered for conversation {res['conversation_id']}, not {resume_id}")
        elif new is None:
            blocked.append("gate check unavailable: agy's transcript of this run is missing or unreadable")
        elif calls[:len(calls_before)] != calls_before or new != seen:
            blocked.append(f"gate hook inactive: {len(seen)} gate decisions for {len(new)} tool calls"
                           f" ({' '.join(seen[:8])} | {' '.join(new[:8])}); inspect anything the worker could reach")
        elif not gate_log and not meta and wt_git(pinned, "status", "--porcelain", *spec(task), check=False):
            blocked.append("gate hook inactive: files changed with no gate decision")
        if quiet > 3:
            warnings.append(f"{quiet} quiet denials (reads of .git or .agents): the worker may be probing the sandbox")
    warnings += [f"{b}; nothing was auto-committed, inspect the worktree" for b in blocked]
    base = pinned["base"]
    changed = "not inspected"
    if not meta:
        def links(out):
            return {line.split("\t", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines() if line.startswith("160000 ")}
        try:  # never lose the agent's work to a hook or signing failure
            if not blocked:
                # git add fails on an exclude that names an ignored path (a repo that gitignores .agents/); add -A
                # skips ignored paths anyway
                wt_git(pinned, "add", "-A", *[x for x in spec(task) if not x.startswith(":(exclude)")
                                              or not wt_git(pinned, "check-ignore", "--", x[10:], check=False)])
                new = links(wt_git(pinned, "ls-files", "-s")) - links(wt_git(pinned, "ls-tree", "-r", "HEAD"))
                if new:  # a backstop for the walk above
                    warnings.append(f"worker staged a new gitlink at {', '.join(sorted(new))}; nothing was auto-committed")
                elif wt_git(pinned, "diff", "--cached", "--name-only", "--no-ext-diff", "--no-textconv"):
                    wt_git(pinned, "commit", "--no-gpg-sign", "--no-verify", "-qm", f"{CLI}: {task.name}")
        except SystemExit as e:
            warnings.append(f"commit failed, changes are uncommitted in the worktree: {e}")
        changed = wt_git(pinned, "diff", "--shortstat", "--no-ext-diff", "--no-textconv", base, "HEAD",
                         check=False) or "no changes"
        if changed == "no changes" and wt_git(pinned, "status", "--porcelain", "--ignore-submodules=all", *spec(task),
                                              check=False):
            changed = "uncommitted changes"
    if not moved_wt and not dotgit_ok(pinned):  # a straggler rewrote it after the restore
        warnings.append("worker modified .git after the run; inspect the worktree")
    denied = res["denied"]
    stopped_by = stopped[0] if stopped else "timeout" if res["timed_out"] or "timeout" in interrupted else None
    review = a.review
    incomplete = any(w.startswith(("interrupted", "timed out", "stopped", "commit failed", "worker ", "git metadata",
                                   "gate "))
                     for w in warnings)
    produced = bool(res["response"].strip()) if review else changed != "no changes"
    ok = res["done"] and not denied and code == 0 and not incomplete and produced
    wall = time.monotonic() - t0
    result = {"ok": ok, "slug": task.name, "model": o.get("model"), "agent": o.get("agent"), "wall_s": round(wall), "branch": f"{CLI}/{task.name}", "worktree": str(wt), "review": review,
              "base": base, "changes": changed, "denied_actions": denied, "quiet_denials": quiet, "warnings": warnings,
              "conversation_id": res["conversation_id"], "stopped_by": stopped_by, "exit_code": code, "usage": res["usage"],
              "response": res["response"], "stderr": err.strip()[-500:]}
    (task / "result.json").write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2))
    u = res["usage"]
    tokens = u.get("total_tokens", sum(v for v in u.values() if isinstance(v, int))) if isinstance(u, dict) and u else None
    dispatch_log("finish", task.name, o.get("model"), ok=ok, denied=len(denied), tokens=tokens,
                 wall_s=round(wall), stopped_by=stopped_by, agent=o.get("agent"))
    hint = " (resume it: file tools on worktree files only, no shell beyond git status/diff/log/show, ls, cat)" if CLI == "agy" else ""
    note = (f" DENIED: {', '.join(denied)}{hint}" if denied else "") \
        + "".join(f" WARNING: {w}" for w in warnings)
    print(f"{PROG} {task.name}: {'ok' if ok else 'NOT ok'} ({changed}){note} -> {task}/result.json")
    return 0 if ok else 1


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawTextHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument("cmd", choices=["start", "resume", "list", "clean"])
    ap.add_argument("slug", nargs="?")
    ap.add_argument("prompt", nargs="?", help="task text, or - to read it from stdin")
    ap.add_argument("--model", default=None)
    ap.add_argument("--effort", help="model variant; default per model, '' for none")
    ap.add_argument("--agent", default=None, help="specialist agent (start only; resume reuses it)")
    ap.add_argument("--timeout", default="20m")
    ap.add_argument("--base", default="HEAD")
    ap.add_argument("--setup", help="shell command run in the worktree before agy (start only)")
    ap.add_argument("--max-denied", type=int, default=10, help="opencode: kill the worker at this many denied commands (0 = off)")
    ap.add_argument("--max-tool-errors", type=int, default=20, help="opencode: kill the worker at this many failed tool calls (0 = off)")
    ap.add_argument("--review", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--yolo", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--force", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--wait", action="store_true", help="queue for a free slot instead of refusing at the limit")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    if a.cmd in ("start", "resume") and os.environ.get("CLAUDECODE") != "1" and os.environ.get("SWARMKIT_ALLOW_WORKERS") != "1":
        print(f"{PROG}: workers are started only by Claude Code (CLAUDECODE=1 missing). In OpenCode or Antigravity, use your own "
              "subagents instead. Set SWARMKIT_ALLOW_WORKERS=1 to start one by hand from a terminal.", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    from_agent = a.model is None and a.cmd == "start" and a.agent and CLI == "opencode"
    if a.model is None:
        a.model = BACKEND["model"]

    if a.cmd == "start" and a.model not in BACKEND["allowed"]:
        print(f"{PROG}: model not on the worker allowlist: {a.model} (allowed: {', '.join(BACKEND['allowed'])})", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)

    if a.cmd == "resume" and a.agent:
        print(f"{PROG}: --agent is for start only; resume reuses the agent of start", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    if a.cmd == "start" and a.agent and CLI == "agy":
        bad = agy_agent_problem(a.agent)
        if bad:
            print(f"{PROG}: {bad}", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
    elif a.cmd == "start" and a.agent:
        if not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*", a.agent):
            print(f"{PROG}: invalid agent name: {a.agent}", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        if a.agent == "lead-dev-hybrid":
            print(f"{PROG}: orchestrators cannot run as workers: lead-dev-hybrid", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        if not (agents_dir() / f"{a.agent}.md").is_file():
            print(f"{PROG}: unknown OpenCode agent: {a.agent}", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        if agent_edits_git(a.agent):
            print(f"{PROG}: agent {a.agent} has an edit rule for .git; it cannot run as a worker", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        if from_agent:
            m = agent_model(a.agent)
            if m in BACKEND["allowed"]:
                a.model = m
            elif m:
                print(f"{PROG}: agent {a.agent} model {m} is not on the worker allowlist; using {a.model}", file=sys.stderr)
    if a.effort is None:
        a.effort = EFFORT_DEFAULTS.get(a.model, "")

    def base(b):  # resolved, so the worktree path git records is the one we check against
        return Path(os.path.realpath(os.environ.get(f"{b['env']}_DIR", Path.home() / b["home"])))
    # Before any git call: from inside a task dir, git here would follow the worker's .git.
    cwd = Path(os.path.realpath(Path.cwd()))
    for b in BACKENDS.values():
        if cwd == base(b) or base(b) in cwd.parents:
            sys.exit(f"{PROG}: run {PROG} from the main checkout, not from inside a task dir ({base(b)})")
    # The first `git worktree list` entry is the main working tree, also when run from a linked
    # worktree or a submodule: it keys the task dirs, so every worktree shares one list and cap.
    # `here` is the checkout we were invoked from: HEAD (default base, merged check) means its HEAD.
    repo = Path(sh("git", "worktree", "list", "--porcelain").splitlines()[0].split(" ", 1)[1])
    here = Path(sh("git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"))
    if a.cmd == "start" and CLI == "agy":  # the gate overlay lives in .agents/, which the gate keeps off limits
        tracked = [f for f in sh("git", "ls-tree", "-r", "--name-only", "-z", a.base, cwd=here, check=False).split("\0")
                   if {c.lower() for c in f.split("/")} & set(AGY_ROOTS)]
        if tracked:
            print(f"{PROG}: {a.base} tracks {tracked[0]}: agy's customization dirs ({', '.join(AGY_ROOTS)}) cannot be in a "
                  "worker's base", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
    key = f"{repo.name}-{hashlib.sha1(str(repo).encode()).hexdigest()[:6]}"
    root = base(BACKEND) / key
    if a.cmd == "list":
        for d in sorted(root.glob("*/")) if root.exists() else []:
            r = json.loads((d / "result.json").read_text()) if (d / "result.json").exists() else {}
            run = alive(d / "pid")
            state = "running" if run else ("ok" if r.get("ok") else "NOT ok" if r else "unfinished")
            print(f"{d.name:18} {state:10} {list_extra(d, r, run)}{r.get('changes', '')}")
        return 0
    if not a.slug or not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,40}", a.slug):
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: slug must be lowercase letters, digits, . _ - (max 41 chars)")
    task, branch = root / a.slug, f"{CLI}/{a.slug}"
    if CLI == "agy" and a.cmd in ("start", "resume") and not a.yolo:
        try:
            v = re.search(r"\d+\.\d+\.\d+", subprocess.run(["agy", "--version"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout)
        except OSError:
            v = None
        if (v and v[0]) != AGY_PROBED and os.environ.get("AGY_TASK_ALLOW_UNPROBED") != "1":
            print(f"{PROG}: agy {v[0] if v else '(version unknown)'} is not the version the gate was probed on"
                  f" ({AGY_PROBED}); its tool names, argument keys or transcript may differ. Re-probe (see 'agy gate'"
                  " in --help) and bump AGY_PROBED, or set AGY_TASK_ALLOW_UNPROBED=1", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)

    if a.cmd == "clean":
        wt = task / "worktree"
        merged = subprocess.run(["git", "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", branch, "HEAD"], cwd=here).returncode == 0
        if not a.force:
            if os.path.lexists(wt):
                p = pin(task, repo)
                if wt_git(p, "status", "--porcelain", "--ignore-submodules=all", *spec(task), check=False):
                    sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {wt} has uncommitted changes; inspect them or pass --force to discard")
                if not dotgit_ok(p):
                    sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {wt / '.git'} was changed since the run; inspect it, or pass --force to discard")
            if not merged:
                sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {branch} is not merged into HEAD; merge it or pass --force to discard")
        # Not `git worktree remove`: it reads <wt>/.git. Delete the tree, then prune drops the gitdir that
        # pointed at it (prune reads only the main repo's worktrees/<id>/gitdir).
        shutil.rmtree(task, ignore_errors=True)
        sh("git", "worktree", "prune", cwd=repo, check=False)
        sh("git", "branch", "-D", branch, cwd=repo, check=False)
        return 0

    # One limit for all backends and all repos: they share the box. The lock makes check-and-claim atomic, so queued
    # --wait callers cannot all see the same free slot; the claim is the pid file written below.
    cap = int(os.environ.get(f"{BACKEND['env']}_MAX", 3))
    lock = open(Path.home() / ".swarmkit-task.lock", "a")
    queued = False
    while True:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        running = [f for b in BACKENDS.values() for f in base(b).glob("*/*/pid") if alive(f)]
        if len(running) < cap:
            break
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        if not a.wait:
            sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {len(running)} delegated tasks already running (all backends and repos); wait for one, or pass --wait")
        if not queued:
            print(f"{PROG} \u25b6 {a.slug} \u00b7 queued ({len(running)} running)", file=sys.stderr)
            queued = True
        time.sleep(10)
    def claim(task):
        (task / "pid").write_text(str(os.getpid()))
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
    prompt = sys.stdin.read() if a.prompt == "-" else a.prompt
    if not prompt:
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: a prompt (or -) is required")
    if a.cmd == "start":
        if task.exists():
            sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {task} exists; pick another slug or run clean")
        try:
            task.mkdir(parents=True)
        except FileExistsError:
            sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {task} exists; pick another slug or run clean")
        claim(task)
        base = sh("git", "rev-parse", a.base, cwd=here)
        (task / "base").write_text(base)
        try:
            sh("git", "-c", "worktree.useRelativePaths=false", "worktree", "add", "-q", "-b", branch,
               str(task / "worktree"), base, cwd=repo)
        except SystemExit:
            for f in task.iterdir():
                f.unlink()
            task.rmdir()
            raise
        # The worker can rewrite <wt>/.git: record where it points now, before anything runs in there.
        wt = task / "worktree"
        (task / "opts.json").write_text(json.dumps({"gitdir": sh("git", "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir", cwd=wt)}))
        (task / "dotgit").write_bytes((wt / ".git").read_bytes())
        p = pin(task, repo)  # also checks that git wrote the .git we expect
        dirty = sh("git", "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=no", cwd=here)
        warn = [f"{here} has uncommitted changes; {CLI} sees only the committed state "
                f"of {a.base}"] if dirty and a.base == "HEAD" else []
        if git_version() < (2, 40):
            warn.append(f"git {'.'.join(map(str, git_version()))} is older than 2.40: no --attr-source, so a"
                        " worker-written .gitattributes can pick a filter from your git config")
        if a.setup:
            sh("sh", "-c", a.setup, cwd=wt)
            # Keep setup artifacts (e.g. a node_modules link) out of agy's commit. Not info/exclude:
            # that file is shared with the main checkout.
            (task / "setup-artifacts").write_text(
                wt_git(p, "ls-files", "--others", "--exclude-standard", "--directory"))
        out = []  # after --setup: tracked symlinks and the ones setup made
        for d, dirs, files in os.walk(wt):
            if d == str(wt):
                dirs[:] = [n for n in dirs if n != ".git"]
            out += [os.path.relpath(f, wt) for f in (os.path.join(d, n) for n in sorted(dirs + files))
                    if os.path.islink(f) and not Path(os.path.realpath(f)).is_relative_to(os.path.realpath(wt))]
        if out:
            warn.append(f"symlinks point outside the worktree ({', '.join(out[:5])}); the gate resolves"
                        f" them and denies {CLI} access through them, but your own test runs follow them")
        for w in warn:
            print(f"{PROG}: WARNING: {w}", file=sys.stderr)
        (task / "nested-git").write_text(json.dumps(nested_gits(wt)))  # setup's own repos are allowed
        return run_task(task, prompt, a, repo, warnings=warn)
    if alive(task / "pid"):
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {a.slug} is still running; wait for it before resuming")
    if not (task / "result.json").exists():
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: no finished run for {a.slug} to resume")
    prev = json.loads((task / "result.json").read_text())
    if not prev.get("conversation_id"):
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: previous run has no conversation_id to resume")
    o = json.loads((task / "opts.json").read_text()) if (task / "opts.json").exists() else {}
    if not o.get("gitdir") or not (task / "dotgit").exists():
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {a.slug} was started before git isolation and cannot be resumed; "
                 f"inspect {task / 'worktree'} by hand, then clean it with --force")
    if not dotgit_ok(pin(task, repo)):
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {task / 'worktree' / '.git'} was changed since the last run; inspect it, then clean it with --force")
    if CLI == "opencode" and o.get("agent") and agent_edits_git(o["agent"]):
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: agent {o['agent']} has an edit rule for .git; it cannot run as a worker")
    if CLI == "agy" and o.get("agent") and agy_agent_problem(o["agent"]):
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {agy_agent_problem(o['agent'])}")
    a.review = a.review or prev.get("review", False)  # a resumed review stays a review
    claim(task)
    return run_task(task, prompt, a, repo, prev["conversation_id"])


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
